<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures steady in quiet market.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures steady in quiet market.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian wheat futures held steady on Thursday with the nearby March 1997 contract rising by 50 cents to A$171.00 a tonne in six trades.</p>
<p>Settlement prices, the mid-point betweenm bid and ask quotes, were mainly steady. Market sources described the market as very quiet with some buying interest at about A$170.00.</p>
<p>Last night's USDA crop report did not influence the Australian market, which remained pegged to the Australian Wheat Board's pool price. &quot;Until that changes there will be no change (in the Australian market)&quot;, they said.  </p>
